name social-chemistry-101-breakdowns
# "The dataset is tab-separated with the following columns" (README), and its first row names them. A row is one
# worker's breakdown of one rule of thumb: it is said of the row's rot-id ("ID of the rule of thumb"), and what the
# row says it says together, so the worker (breakdown-worker-id) and the worker's answers stay in one record.
# README: rot-categorization, rot-moral-foundations and characters are each a '"|" separated list'.
# The file writes a field that holds a double quote between double quotes, with the quote doubled (4,927 rows).
# The table reader does not read that notation, so those rows are left unread rather than recorded as written.
match social-chem-101.v1.0.tsv
grammar table
header
list rot-categorization |
list rot-moral-foundations |
list characters |

claims
together
# A rule of thumb is its text; its situation is the text it was written for. The ids, worker ids, split and counts are
# the set's bookkeeping, read by nothing.
key rot-id situation-short-id rot-worker-id breakdown-worker-id
subject in rot
attest situation area rot-agree rot-categorization rot-moral-foundations rot-char-targeting rot-bad rot-judgment action action-agency action-moral-judgment action-agree action-legal action-pressure action-char-involved action-hypothetical characters
where situation matches ^($|[^"])
where characters matches ^($|[^"])
where rot matches ^($|[^"])
where action matches ^($|[^"])
where rot-judgment matches ^($|[^"])
